---
layout: layouts/base.njk
---
{#
  layouts/workspace.njk
  ---------------------
  The workspace picture, filling the whole window. It is 60 pictures taken as
  a camera pans across the scene in Blender (assets/img/workspace/0001.webp
  to 0060.webp); assets/js/workspace.js shows the one that matches where the
  mouse is, so moving the mouse left and right looks around the room.

  Settings on the canvas:
        data-frames   how many pictures there are
        data-path     the folder they are in
        data-ext      their file type (webp, jpg...)
        data-invert   "true" to flip the direction

  The dots come from the "spots" list in src/workspace-temp.md, which can also
  be edited in /admin under Pages. Each one needs x and y (where it is in the
  picture, 0 to 1) and the number of the picture those were measured on; the
  script keeps it on its item as the room turns. To place new ones, open the
  page with ?place at the end of the address.

  A dot with a "link" leads there when it is clicked: a page of this site
  (like /projects/) or a full web address, which opens in a new tab. On a
  phone the first tap opens the words and the second one follows the link.

  Each dot can also carry either a few photos that loop, or one small video
  (an uploaded file or a YouTube link). They play by themselves and cannot be
  clicked.
#}
<h1 class="visually-hidden">{{ title }}</h1>

<canvas class="ws" data-workspace
        data-frames="60"
        data-path="{{ '/assets/img/workspace/' | url }}"
        data-ext="webp"
        data-invert="false"
        role="img"
        aria-label="An interactive view of the workspace. Move the mouse left and right, up and down, to look around."></canvas>
<p class="ws__status" data-workspace-status aria-live="polite"></p>

{% if spots %}
<div class="ws-spots" data-spots>
  {% for spot in spots %}
  {% set kind = spot.media or ("photos" if spot.images else ("video" if (spot.youtube or spot.video) else "")) %}
  <div class="ws-spot{% if spot.link %} has-link{% endif %}" data-spot
       data-x="{{ spot.x }}"
       data-y="{{ spot.y }}"
       data-frame="{{ spot.frame or 0 }}"
       {% if spot.depth %}data-depth="{{ spot.depth }}"{% endif %}>
    <button class="ws-spot__dot" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="ws-spot-{{ loop.index }}">
      <span class="visually-hidden">{{ spot.title }}{% if spot.text %}. {{ spot.text }}{% endif %}</span>
    </button>

    <div class="ws-spot__card" id="ws-spot-{{ loop.index }}" aria-hidden="true">
      {# The words are written out one letter at a time by workspace.js; they
         start empty and live in the data-type attribute. #}
      <p class="ws-spot__title" data-type="{{ spot.title }}"></p>
      {% if spot.text %}<p class="ws-spot__text" data-type="{{ spot.text }}"></p>{% endif %}
      {% if spot.link %}
      {% set external = spot.link.startsWith("http") %}
      <a class="ws-spot__go" data-type="{{ 'Visit link >' if external else 'Open page >' }}"
         href="{{ spot.link if external else (spot.link | url) }}"
         {% if external %}target="_blank" rel="noopener"{% endif %}
         aria-label="{{ spot.title }}: {{ 'open link' if external else 'open page' }}"></a>
      {% endif %}

      {% if kind == "photos" and spot.images %}
      <div class="ws-spot__media ws-spot__media--photos">
        {% for shot in spot.images %}
        <img class="ws-spot__shot{% if loop.first %} is-on{% endif %}" src="{{ (shot.image or shot) | url }}" alt="" loading="lazy">
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      {% elif kind == "video" and spot.video %}
      <div class="ws-spot__media ws-spot__media--video">
        <video data-video muted loop playsinline preload="none" src="{{ spot.video | url }}"></video>
      </div>
      {% elif kind == "video" and spot.youtube %}
      {% set videoId = spot.youtube | youtubeId %}
      {% if videoId %}
      <div class="ws-spot__media ws-spot__media--video">
        {# The address is only put in place once the dot is opened, so nothing
           loads from YouTube until then. #}
        <iframe data-yt="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/{{ videoId }}?autoplay=1&mute=1&loop=1&playlist={{ videoId }}&controls=0&modestbranding=1&rel=0&playsinline=1&iv_load_policy=3&disablekb=1&fs=0&enablejsapi=1"
                title="" tabindex="-1" frameborder="0" allow="autoplay; encrypted-media"></iframe>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
{% endif %}

{# Only shown when the address ends in ?place. #}
<div class="ws-place" data-place>
  <h2>Placing dots</h2>
  <p>Move the mouse to turn the room, then click an item to drop a dot on it. Copy the result into the spots list in src/workspace-temp.md.</p>
  <span class="ws-place__readout" data-place-readout>Move the mouse over the room</span>
  <span class="ws-place__list" data-place-list></span>
  <button type="button" data-place-copy>Copy</button>
  <button type="button" data-place-undo>Undo</button>
</div>
